# More info: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
#
# Deliberately an exclude list rather than the "ignore ** then re-include" style
# the scaffold ships with. That style relies on the builder descending into
# excluded directories to evaluate ! exceptions, which BuildKit does and the
# classic builder does not — so with the classic builder you get an empty
# context and a confusing "package cmd/main.go is not in std" at build time.

# Build output and local tooling
bin/
dist/
cover.out

# VCS and editor noise
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Not needed to build the manager
test/e2e/
*.md
